  "lineage": "Khaliji (\"Gulf\") urban popular music of the Arabian Peninsula Gulf states — Kuwait, Bahrain, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, UAE, Oman — characterized by mid-tempo 2/4 or 4/4 metric base with syncopated 2-and-4 backbeat and distinctive Khaliji-modal vocabulary between maqam-Arabic and Persian-dastgah. The genre developed from the older sawt classical urban-chamber Bahraini-and-Kuwaiti tradition into contemporary Khaliji-pop through the post-1970s petroleum-era recording industry centered in Bahrain, Kuwait, and Riyadh.",
